Z||000000||Greg Piet||03-04-2001||06:37 PM||||This is from another topic...<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowCG:<BR><B>In the fifties they were called "greasers",now they're ricers,whatever.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I always thought Greasers actually worked on their car and made it run better/faster.<BR>ex: Installed headers with dual straight pipes<P>I always thought ricers paid people to work on their car and made it run worse/slower.<BR>ex: paid a mechanic to install a 4" chrome muffler tip on a 1.5" stock exhaust<P>now I was not alive in the 50's but people from that era tell me I would have been a greaser, so I guess I am a ricer. <BR><P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">  <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
