Z||000007||Cheever2||03-05-2001||10:19 PM||||Gotta set the record straight.  Tulsa native S. E. Hinton denied that there was any real history as the basis for her book, <I>The Outsiders</I>.  But everybody who grew up in North Tulsa in the 50's & 60's knows different.  As someone posted, Greasers were those who slicked their hair back.  They were from the wrong side of the tracks (Northsiders).  Soc's (no it's not pronounced "socks", but rather it's short for "socialites") were the Southsiders who were middle to upper class and regarded the Greasers as less than human.  I don't know of any rumble they ever won, however.  Tulsa has since grown much farther South, but at the time, Soc's were anyone living South of Admiral Boulevard.  The drive-in theatre in the story was the Admiral Twin, which had a movie on each side of the screen, each parking area facing the other, East & West.  Each side had a playground up by the screen for the kiddies, and a concession stand with a few rows of seats in front of the projectionist's booth.  Francis Ford Coppola used the exact location for the movie.  He filmed the Greasers' house at a little town just North of Tulsa called Sperry, whose pride was the one stop sign that didn't have a bullet hole in it.  That's where I went to high school.  The closest real life person to the Ponyboy character that I know of would have been my older brother, but I doubt Ms. Hinton knew him (she lived just a few blocks South of Admiral Blvd).  He worked at the drive-in, and we experienced the greatest waterballoon fight in history, fought by the theatre employees one hot summer night after the customers left (East vs. West).  My brother & I were on the winning side; it ended just before dawn.  I can post his website.  He's into Harleys.<P>Uh, what was the question?<P><BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
Z||000008||Cheever2||03-06-2001||12:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>I think a far more accurate name for people who spend theirmodification budget on non-functional wannabe "performance" stuff would be "posers"...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> How about changing that slightly to "importsters"?<P><BR>||||reg||1
